{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7","id":1547294,"title":"Has anyone ever tried to fix Presence 7?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-27T23:52:33-08:00","id":1547294,"title":"Has anyone ever tried to fix Presence 7?","content":"I mean, when we look at Advanced Powers, it seems always weird that Presence is a discipline where all the level 7 powers are weird and strictly situational, while we have many great examples of level 6 (<i>Love</i>, <i>Paralyzing Glance)</i> it feels weird when the next level feels like a downgrade, I mean wtf is <i>Cooperation!?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T21:18:14-08:00","id":1547472,"title":"","content":"You know I haven't tried to work with any high level Presence abilities despite it being one of my top Disciplines I like. But as I pointed out in other posts the lowest generation I ever played was the 7th. Maybe I will come with cool Amalgam powers that use the Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T21:25:47-08:00","id":1547474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547472#post1547472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I haven't tried to work with any high level Presence abilities despite it being one of my top Disciplines I like. But as I pointed out in other posts the lowest generation I ever played was the 7th. Maybe I will come with cool Amalgam powers that use the Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. This fact is a rather curious one, because as I have created many stories for elders over the years, whenever I have a player who wants (and naturally can) to buy Presence 7, there's always this &quot;problem&quot;, that while they're reading the powers it seems level 7 wasn't really thought much about, all of the powers created for level 7 are quite terrible, especially in comparisson with many of the awesome ones we have at level 6. So, in this case basically any idea is welcomed, as I believe we have many storytellers here I thought about asking to see if anyone has come up with ideas for advanced Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T00:47:10-08:00","id":1547479,"title":"","content":"Characters that advance beyond lvl 5 powers don't usually know all the powers that are possible, they usually start developing them as they see fit for their own situation.<br /> If a player wants to invest in a presence 7 power and none of the pre-made point sinks are fitting, I'd ask him what exactly it is he would like to accomplish, then adjust that desired power to the appropriate level, adding or substracting some checks or effects where needed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T00:57:57-08:00","id":1547480,"title":"","content":"How about something that makes the previous levels much easier to roll, meaning statistically more successes, meaning narratively more consistent and impressive results when Presence is used?<br /> For example, Presence 1 is nice, but getting 5 successes on a diff. 7 roll to influence the whole room with a dice pool of 14 dice maximum (for vamps who can reach 7 dots in each trait) is rare. The average is 4.2 successes, and that's with the maximum dice pool. One could go heavy handedly to Majesty, but it's not the same and it's not subtle at all. The other powers have similar statistical limits, somewhat lessened for those where the difficulty depend on the victim's traits, if they have low traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-03T12:56:11-08:00","id":1547497,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> idea is good, especially because it's easier to use &quot;a precedent&quot; when developping a power. While what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26274_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26274\" data-vbnamecard=\"26274\">Moriaki</a> said is naturally to be taken into consideration, normally don't want to delve too much into it as we'd need in order to create a power from scratch, so it's always more convenient to see what powers were already created or, in other words, &quot;to use a precedent&quot; as I was saying. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> idea of making a more powerful version of <i>Awe</i> is interesting, some players have asked me in the past to make a more powerful version of <i>Paralyzing Glance</i>, but then I refuted at the time, because the level 6 power is already very powerful on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T01:18:15-08:00","id":1547511,"title":"","content":"Maybe look at level 7 powers from other Disciplines and adapt something? E.g., two of the Melpominee 7 powers let you leave a song/melody behind to affect someone later, or to leave your voice behind to do the same. Maybe Presence 7 could leave a lingering presence behind to affect someone who comes into contact with it later?<br /> <br /> The level 7 Presence power which lets you influence your descendants to frenzy could be adjusted to provide other effects to your descendants, or perhaps people who are blood bonded to you\u2014or even just people you've affected with Presence previously.<br /> <br /> Serpentis 7: Divine Presence could be an interesting model. You could have the vampire appear as a god or other supernatural entity, complete with the appearance of having any powers and qualities that being could have (Aphrodite makes all men fall in love with her, Mars makes people warlike, Cthulhu sends people mad, while Hercules may not be super strong if the vampire isn't but can make people believe he is, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T11:43:42-08:00","id":1547520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547511#post1547511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe look at level 7 powers from other Disciplines and adapt something? E.g., two of the Melpominee 7 powers let you leave a song/melody behind to affect someone later, or to leave your voice behind to do the same. Maybe Presence 7 could leave a lingering presence behind to affect someone who comes into contact with it later?<br /> <br /> The level 7 Presence power which lets you influence your descendants to frenzy could be adjusted to provide other effects to your descendants, or perhaps people who are blood bonded to you\u2014or even just people you've affected with Presence previously.<br /> <br /> Serpentis 7: Divine Presence could be an interesting model. You could have the vampire appear as a god or other supernatural entity, complete with the appearance of having any powers and qualities that being could have (Aphrodite makes all men fall in love with her, Mars makes people warlike, Cthulhu sends people mad, while Hercules may not be super strong if the vampire isn't but can make people believe he is, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a good idea. In fact now that you mention this Serpentis power serves as an idea, even though the power itself is among the worst offenders in the history of &quot;shitty advanced discipline powers&quot;. Here of course I mean the system, the description is really interesting on a narrative level and all, but the system would be bad for a level 3 power lol, let alone a level 7, seems like a bad joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T20:20:34-08:00","id":1547532,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that originally only the level 1-5 powers of a Discipline were &quot;standard&quot;. At level 6 and above, characters could develop their own powers of that Discipline rank. Elder NPCs who were generation 7 and stronger who had Disciplines at 6+ always had a description bloc of what their specific Discipline at those ranks. Thus powers are often very particular to what that NPC wanted. As originally written, PCs could not normally learn those Disciplines because their generation was too weak so there wasn't a need to provide anything for players except as a rare exception.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of Rank 6+ Disciplines in the Revised sourcebooks were mainly taken from existing canon NPCs that existed in earlier editions, and anything that was missing was simply filled in using those examples as guidelines.<br /> <br /> So I see the description of level 6+ powers simply as a rough guide to use for STs and PCs when designing their own powers. If you don't like a power, create something you do like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T21:21:38-08:00","id":1547534,"title":"","content":"That's what I do for Amalgam powers in our game and I do like creating level 6 Discipline abilities and the only exception was the Blood Scrying power that the 3rd generation would definitely use. Though I could see elders and older ancillae trying to learn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T21:56:42-08:00","id":1547537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547532#post1547532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember that originally only the level 1-5 powers of a Discipline were &quot;standard&quot;. At level 6 and above, characters could develop their own powers of that Discipline rank. Elder NPCs who were generation 7 and stronger who had Disciplines at 6+ always had a description bloc of what their specific Discipline at those ranks. Thus powers are often very particular to what that NPC wanted. As originally written, PCs could not normally learn those Disciplines because their generation was too weak so there wasn't a need to provide anything for players except as a rare exception.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of Rank 6+ Disciplines in the Revised sourcebooks were mainly taken from existing canon NPCs that existed in earlier editions, and anything that was missing was simply filled in using those examples as guidelines.<br /> <br /> So I see the description of level 6+ powers simply as a rough guide to use for STs and PCs when designing their own powers. If you don't like a power, create something you do like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, but then after that they kind of took a life of their own. One nice info about it though, is that they nerfed Dieter Kotlar's &quot;Burning Wrath&quot; when they created the Celerity and Potence combo as the part where you need to test your willpower in order to act after being hit by the power wasn't included in the combo discipline afterwards. I also like the idea of using powers created as guidelines, but I can't help not noticing which ones have good system and the others who are terrible and weak. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what I do for Amalgam powers in our game and I do like creating level 6 Discipline abilities and the only exception was the Blood Scrying power that the 3rd generation would definitely use. Though I could see elders and older ancillae trying to learn it. </div> </div> </div>Cool, I love to do that as well, but creating new powers requires a good time investment and often it's easier to simply get the ones who were made and focus in the story. By the way, I love reading about powers, would you care to share the powers you've developped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T22:34:45-08:00","id":1547540,"title":"","content":"I can do that as I have the notes in a folder in my list of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T10:57:21-08:00","id":1547549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547540#post1547540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can do that as I have the notes in a folder in my list of characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be really cool, but I unfortunately couldn't send you a private message, the forum's system said you don't receive private messages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T13:26:33-08:00","id":1547552,"title":"","content":"No problem Herr Meister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T13:38:15-08:00","id":1547553,"title":"","content":"Here's the first Amalgam power I created for my Malkavian character.<br /> <br /> Shared Resilience came about because I thought that good help is hard to find and smart kindred wouldn't needlessly sacrifice assets needlessly.<br /> <br /> Shared Resilience Fortitude 2 and Auspex 3<br /> . Prequistes: Shared Senses/Toughness<br /> Cost: 1 Rouse Check<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina+Auspex<br /> System: The Kindred can choose to extend some of their Fortitude powers to Ghouls/Humans affected by there Auspex. Anyone thus anyone imbued gains additional health equal to the fortitude dots of said Kindred.<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> <br /> My character likes to use this ability alot as he still cares about his agents be it ghouls or freelancers that have impressed him with their work. It's useful and not to over the top.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T19:01:16-08:00","id":1547568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547553#post1547553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the first Amalgam power I created for my Malkavian character.<br /> <br /> Shared Resilience came about because I thought that good help is hard to find and smart kindred wouldn't needlessly sacrifice assets needlessly.<br /> <br /> Shared Resilience Fortitude 2 and Auspex 3<br /> . Prequistes: Shared Senses/Toughness<br /> Cost: 1 Rouse Check<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina+Auspex<br /> System: The Kindred can choose to extend some of their Fortitude powers to Ghouls/Humans affected by there Auspex. Anyone thus anyone imbued gains additional health equal to the fortitude dots of said Kindred.<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> <br /> My character likes to use this ability alot as he still cares about his agents be it ghouls or freelancers that have impressed him with their work. It's useful and not to over the top.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very cool and interesting power, reminds me of Martyr's Resilience from <i>Guide to the Camarilla</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T07:46:05-08:00","id":1547581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547520#post1547520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's also a good idea. In fact now that you mention this Serpentis power serves as an idea, even though the power itself is among the worst offenders in the history of &quot;shitty advanced discipline powers&quot;. Here of course I mean the system, the description is really interesting on a narrative level and all, but the system would be bad for a level 3 power lol, let alone a level 7, seems like a bad joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're all weak. I usually turn 6+ Discipline powers into Combo Disciplines for much lower levels. I rather liked the way Mage and Mummy dealt with traits over 5.<br /> <br /> If you prefer, you can just make Disciplines 6+ work as permanent modifiers to range, duration, etc, or as ways to &quot;break&quot; the rules of a Discipline (I'm pretty sure I've outlined that approach here before, actually). So, if a five-dot Discipline allows you to affect a city block, the six-dot Discipline would let you affect a whole neighborhood. Seven dots would affect a whole city, while eight would affect a US state or small country, and nine would affect the entire Eastern Seaboard or, say, Mesopotamia (perfect for the elders...).<br /> <br /> Other Disciplines might scale in similar ways. Dominate might be able to work through &quot;degrees of separation&quot;, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:59:12-08:00","id":1547599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547581#post1547581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they're all weak. I usually turn 6+ Discipline powers into Combo Disciplines for much lower levels. I rather liked the way Mage and Mummy dealt with traits over 5.<br /> <br /> If you prefer, you can just make Disciplines 6+ work as permanent modifiers to range, duration, etc, or as ways to &quot;break&quot; the rules of a Discipline (I'm pretty sure I've outlined that approach here before, actually). So, if a five-dot Discipline allows you to affect a city block, the six-dot Discipline would let you affect a whole neighborhood. Seven dots would affect a whole city, while eight would affect a US state or small country, and nine would affect the entire Eastern Seaboard or, say, Mesopotamia (perfect for the elders...).<br /> <br /> Other Disciplines might scale in similar ways. Dominate might be able to work through &quot;degrees of separation&quot;, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is that Advanced Discipline powers is a crazy mixed bag. You have &quot;\u00fcberpowers&quot; like <i>Far Mastery</i> and <i>Ironclad Command</i>, you have good powers like <i>Flesh of Marble</i> or <i>Paralizyng Glance</i> and then you have total worthless &quot;mull&quot; bs like <i>Fiery Agony</i>, <i>Divine Image</i>, <i>Cooperation </i> or <i>The Darkness Within</i>. Unfortunately, the latter category is more prevalent. Your idea is something I've been working on more or less, to give permanent modifiers to the use of powers, I once made the same with Thaumaturgy Paths being used by characters with advanced Blood Sorcery levels. To make other powers more efficient/and/or affecting more targets/a larger area, etc. is a good solution and most of the time better than the Advanced Powers already developed. Interestingly enough, this recent book for V5 gives many interesting idas for powers used by elders/Methusalehs/Blood Gods. One of the first suggestions is exactly to make a power that normally affect only one target to be able to affect multiple targets when used by an &quot;Ancient&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T12:47:53-08:00","id":1547602,"title":"","content":"This is Amalgam power was a tough one to make and I keep on thinking that it should be the property of Blood God's and Methuselah's and not have elders know it. So here goes.<br /> <br /> Blood Scrying Auspex: 5, Obfuscate 4<br /> Prerequiste: Share the Senses<br /> Cost: Two Rouse Checks.<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve+Auspex<br /> <br /> System: Roll resolve at difficulty 1 to target a direct childe of your lineage as per share the senses. The difficulty increases by one for every generation your target is from you.<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 scene.<br /> <br /> I came up with this power thinking of how the 3rd generation and their children and grandchildren could keep track of the clan discreetly and learn of possible threats or insights they could glean. I got the idea from a high level Dominate power that the 4th generation could use to influence their line to do things without any notice.<br /> <br /> With the book Gehenna War out, I've been thinking that it would work better as a Blood God and Methuselah power and not even a 6th generation kindred should know it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T13:21:17-08:00","id":1547605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547602#post1547602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Amalgam power was a tough one to make and I keep on thinking that it should be the property of Blood God's and Methuselah's and not have elders know it. So here goes.<br /> <br /> Blood Scrying Auspex: 5, Obfuscate 4<br /> Prerequiste: Share the Senses<br /> Cost: Two Rouse Checks.<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve+Auspex<br /> <br /> System: Roll resolve at difficulty 1 to target a direct childe of your lineage as per share the senses. The difficulty increases by one for every generation your target is from you.<br /> <br /> Duration: 1 scene.<br /> <br /> I came up with this power thinking of how the 3rd generation and their children and grandchildren could keep track of the clan discreetly and learn of possible threats or insights they could glean. I got the idea from a high level Dominate power that the 4th generation could use to influence their line to do things without any notice.<br /> <br /> With the book Gehenna War out, I've been thinking that it would work better as a Blood God and Methuselah power and not even a 6th generation kindred should know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting power. It's something I sometimes make &quot;without a proper system&quot;, especially for notorious Tremere (as the Clan is by far the most tightly organized), to make the &quot;ancients&quot; of a clan to keep track of its lineage is something really interesting (and something that already appeared in th Clan Novels, one good example is when Etrius use Jervais...). I wonder what level of Auspex I'd make that be, but I agree with you that it should be only acessible to Methuselah and above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T09:13:59-08:00","id":1547617,"title":"","content":"I got the basic premise from the revised Tziscme clan sourcebook where Ruthhaven being the only clan member who saw what really happened during the Anarch Revolt. What a good idea of how scary it would be that the eldest members of the clans all have a variation of this power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T15:51:29-08:00","id":1547624,"title":"","content":"Emotional Mask bis another Amalgam power that my Malkavian created as he learned that there are beings besides his clan that can see Auras and what emotions they hint at and he came up with a ability to hide his true state and project another.<br /> <br /> Emotional Mask<br /> Fortitude 3 and Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: One Rouse Check.<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Obfuscate vs Auspex &amp; Wits Prequistes: Fortify Inner Facade/ Mask of Thousand Faces..<br /> <br /> A simple power used by Kindred who seek to mask their aura and present whatever combination of colors and states they wish to present.<br /> <br /> System: A stamina + Obfuscate roll vs wits and Auspex at difficulty 4 as the vampire can choose the projection of a single aura color that they are familiar. An automatic failure if used to mimic the aura of other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bDuration: One scene.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-07T21:27:54-08:00","id":1547628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547624#post1547624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emotional Mask bis another Amalgam power that my Malkavian created as he learned that there are beings besides his clan that can see Auras and what emotions they hint at and he came up with a ability to hide his true state and project another.<br /> <br /> Emotional Mask<br /> Fortitude 3 and Obfuscate 3<br /> Cost: One Rouse Check.<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Obfuscate vs Auspex &amp; Wits Prequistes: Fortify Inner Facade/ Mask of Thousand Faces..<br /> <br /> A simple power used by Kindred who seek to mask their aura and present whatever combination of colors and states they wish to present.<br /> <br /> System: A stamina + Obfuscate roll vs wits and Auspex at difficulty 4 as the vampire can choose the projection of a single aura color that they are familiar. An automatic failure if used to mimic the aura of other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bDuration: One scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's yet another very interesting power. I've always felt that one shouldn't need level 6 Obfuscate to hide their auras. And yes indeed, it enhances the &quot;Cosmic Horror&quot; feel when you're never sure of how much are the elders capable of seeeing inside of you or what you do, etc. It's great for creating an atmosphere of fear. Also, in combination with other powers one ancient could suddenly not only watch what you do, but take control of you, in fact you begin to question how much of what you do you do out of your own free will...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-10T13:19:53-08:00","id":1547668,"title":"","content":"This one was my attempt to rework a Dark Ages Malkavian power and enhanced for my homebrewed 4th generation Methuselah.<br /> <br /> Prophecy Auspex 5/Dominate 4<br /> Cost: 2 Rouse Check <br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence+Auspex<br /> Prequistes: Premonition/Compel<br /> <br /> Mostly used by members of the Malkavian clan who zealously keep this ability to themselves. The Malkavians use this power to gain insight into possible events based on choices they or other kindred will make and choose the best possible outcome.<br /> <br /> System: Make an Intelligence+Auspex roll vs a difficulty depending on how far into a potential future outcome. Roll At difficulty 2 for immediate outcomes based on a few days or months. Roll at difficulty 3 for years and roll at difficulty 4 for decades/centuries down the road.<br /> <br /> Duration: A few minutes for the immediate future and up to a night for deeper glimpses.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T17:39:25-08:00","id":1547689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547668#post1547668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one was my attempt to rework a Dark Ages Malkavian power and enhanced for my homebrewed 4th generation Methuselah.<br /> <br /> Prophecy Auspex 5/Dominate 4<br /> Cost: 2 Rouse Check<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence+Auspex<br /> Prequistes: Premonition/Compel<br /> <br /> Mostly used by members of the Malkavian clan who zealously keep this ability to themselves. The Malkavians use this power to gain insight into possible events based on choices they or other kindred will make and choose the best possible outcome.<br /> <br /> System: Make an Intelligence+Auspex roll vs a difficulty depending on how far into a potential future outcome. Roll At difficulty 2 for immediate outcomes based on a few days or months. Roll at difficulty 3 for years and roll at difficulty 4 for decades/centuries down the road.<br /> <br /> Duration: A few minutes for the immediate future and up to a night for deeper glimpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting power, I just wonder why the need for Dominate to learn such power. I have a love/hate relationship with Prophecy powers (like <i>Eyes of Chaos</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-11T21:56:47-08:00","id":1547690,"title":"","content":"I felt that the Malkavians are forcing their will upon reality to foresee possible future events. Hence the use of Dominate, and in fact in the Dark Ages section of the Malkavian powers that I rewrote for this section was that Dementation was needed and I'm not a fan of that Discipline.<br /> <br /> I still felt that a mental power was needed to glean probable events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-12-2025, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T14:03:09-08:00","id":1547703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547294-has-anyone-ever-tried-to-fix-presence-7?p=1547690#post1547690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt that the Malkavians are forcing their will upon reality to foresee possible future events. Hence the use of Dominate, and in fact in the Dark Ages section of the Malkavian powers that I rewrote for this section was that Dementation was needed and I'm not a fan of that Discipline.<br /> <br /> I still felt that a mental power was needed to glean probable events.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also not a big fan of Dementation, I consider it a somewhat strange Discipline. In any case, I think Prophecy is totally within the realms of Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-18T13:47:39-08:00","id":1547818,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree and I won't use Dementation for my character and not even as a Amalgam option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}